<title>INDIA: India approves SAIL's tie-up with Russian partners.</title>
<headline>India approves SAIL's tie-up with Russian partners.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>India on Thursday approved a joint venture between state-run Steel Authority of India Ltd (SAIL) and three Russian partners to market a specialised iron making technology, a government statement said.</p>
<p>It said the 10 million rupees joint venture will be set up by SAIL, Amet Ltd, Moscow Institute of Steel and Alloys and Novolipetsk Steel Works.</p>
<p>SAIL will hold 40 percent equity in the joint venture.</p>
<p>The initial issued capital for the joint venture will be 1.2 million rupees, with SAIL contributing 480,000 rupees, the statement said.</p>
</text>
